#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# scorer_hi_prime

#% text
# `scorer_hi_prime(z)` gives the derivative of the Scorer function `Hi(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `Hi'(z) = 3^(-1/3)/pi sum_k gamma((k + 2)/3) (3^(1/3) z)^k/k!` (DLMF 9.12); `Hi'(0) = 2 Bi'(0)/3`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
scorer_hi_prime(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.9808737086542799

#% cell
n(scorer_hi_prime(-2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.054115969989704779963041965756215530

#% cell
scorer_hi_prime(0)
#% output
#= 2*3^(1/6)/(3*gamma(1/3))

#% text
# The equation `Hi'' = z Hi + 1/pi`, checked with a difference quotient of the derivative:

#% cell
z0 = 0.8; h = 1.0e-5; (scorer_hi_prime(z0 + h) - scorer_hi_prime(z0 - h))/(2*h) - z0*scorer_hi(z0) - 1/pi
#% output
#= 3.666766890120243e-11

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `scorer_hi`, `scorer_gi_prime`, `airy_bi_prime`
